Q: What is the difference between tokenization and embedding?

Tokenization converts text into discrete tokens and token IDs. Embedding maps each token ID to a learned numerical vector.
Tokenization identifies the units; embedding provides the vectors the neural network processes.

Q: Why does a Transformer need positional encoding or another positional mechanism?

Self-attention calculates relationships among token representations, but the attention operation alone does not tell the model the original order of the sequence. 
Positional mechanisms provide information about token positions, helping the model distinguish different arrangements of the same tokens.


